# Supabase cloud backup. Copy this file to .env.local and fill in real values.
#
# Both come from Supabase: Project Settings -> API.
#   URL              https://<ref>.supabase.co
#   Publishable key  sb_publishable_...   (this is the key formerly called "anon")
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* values are inlined into the JS bundle at build time and are public by
# design — row level security is what protects the data. Never put the secret key
# (sb_secret_..., formerly service_role) here: the account-deletion Edge Function is
# the only thing that needs it, and Supabase injects it there automatically.
#
# For EAS builds, register the same variables as EAS environment variables:
#   eas env:create --name EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL --value https://<ref>.supabase.co
# EAS Build respects .gitignore, so an ignored .env.local alone would produce a build
# with no backend configured.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Legacy alternative, still accepted if your project predates publishable keys.
# Set one or the other, not both.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Store compliance. Both pages must be publicly reachable before submission, and the
# privacy policy must also be linked from App Store Connect and Play Console.
# Play additionally requires a web-accessible account deletion URL of its own.
EXPO_PUBLIC_PRIVACY_POLICY_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_ACCOUNT_DELETION_URL=
